{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help","id":267348,"title":"Dragon Blood Charms Help!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-28T05:49:41-07:00","id":267348,"title":"Dragon Blood Charms Help!","content":"Hi, I am pretty new to exalted and have encountered a 'problem' in my game, and was hoping those more well-read than I could help me find what I need.<br /> <br /> I won't bore you with the current story details; other than that I am playing an Eclipse and I'm currently trying to stop an N/A manse from exploding. (Specifically, Lookshy)<br /> <br /> Now, I have 10 days in game to do this.<br /> <br /> I've been told that it can't be done in the time frame (Basically, we need to cap a demense) without a solar craftsman or sorcery. I disagree, as by the rules- the time to make something is reduced by the hands involved (many hands make light work, etc) and I can get the MANPOWER to construct it; source the materials fine, transportation is not an issue--<br /> <br /> My issue is the DESIGN rule. It says in the core book that to design a manse it takes a month MINIMUM (page 133). I have 10 days for it to be FINISHED. <br /> <br /> My math worked it out to 51,600 people building, can get it constructed in 10 days. If I employ the entire population of Lookshy helots (and dragonblooded thaumaturges etc ) that will by RAW get it done in 5 days or less.<br /> <br /> How can I, using Dragonblooded ONLY charms, or thaumaturgy rituals, push the design time down? I have access to a LOT of specialized help, it can be assumed someone in the characters social circles will have these charms.<br /> <br /> Are there any spirit charms?<br /> <br /> I have the Bureaucracy 2nd excellency only, otherwise I would attempt speed the wheels.<br /> <br /> Dragonbloods are known for the fact that they work best in groups. I know there is an excellency that adds successes to OTHER people (Dragon-Blooded have access to a special Charm, Terrestrial (Ability) Reinforcement, which allows a Dragon-Blood to temporarily boost the Ability traits of other characters with whom he is allied) but I don't know what else I'm looking for. Craft, Lore, Occult, Bureaucracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2556-firstaide","name":"Firstaide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T06:46:34-07:00","id":267381,"title":"","content":"If your Circle is a Murder Hobo one then there is Amalion, a Manse-focus Third Circle Demon that get summoned into Creation if an architect received a commission so hard that he has to kill himself. Just make her (relatively easy) escape clause happen then bargain with her so she will save the Manse (she likes beautiful architecture and Manse).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T08:08:02-07:00","id":267413,"title":"","content":"To prevent a manse from exploding, as long as it's exploding due to geomantic reasons and not due to an inherent feature of the manse, all you need to do is place the appropriate capstones. Five of them, totally a Resources 5 cost, are placed at appropriate places, determined by a Perception + Lore roll at a difficulty of 1. That's it. No more explosion, you're free to work on the Manse, repairing it, for the months it requires, though proper repairs take far less time than actual construction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1910-seconis","user":"Seconis","date":".  Removed inaccuracy. 09-28-2014, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1910-seconis","name":"Seconis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T08:20:18-07:00","id":267416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=267413#post267413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, he doesn't have access to Solar Circle Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>The escape clause is how demons can leave Malfeas without being summoned through sorcery.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T08:45:06-07:00","id":267434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firstaide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help#post267348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am playing an Eclipse and I'm currently trying to stop an N/A manse from exploding. (Specifically, Lookshy)<br /> <br /> Now, I have 10 days in game to do this.<br /> <br /> I've been told that it can't be done in the time frame</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you, perhaps, being set up to fail and the plot is actually on rails?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T15:08:32-07:00","id":267713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=267434#post267434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you, perhaps, being set up to fail and the plot is actually on rails?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even if that is true, that isn't a reason not to try one's hardest. It is the more experienced players who have said it can't be done, not the GM. I have faith (or maybe just blind hope) that 10 thousand people can achieve the impossible if they work together. It's just that freaking 'minimum 1 month' design rule. I need a way around that, or more details on what is 'design'; and whether using the Dragonblood charms like &quot;with one mind&quot; (lingustics tree) could help.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2556-firstaide","name":"Firstaide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T16:39:44-07:00","id":267752,"title":"","content":"Since the manse is a pre-existing one, could you possibly find the designs for it in Lookshy's archives and use them to reverse-engineer it?<br /> <br /> An Essence 6+ god could feasibly use Chrysalis of Preservation to halt the manse's breakdown while you work, although it might take longer to find such a god and get them to do it than you have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T18:38:30-07:00","id":267799,"title":"","content":"Can you not use craft-speeding Charms on the design phase? Makes little sense to be able to speed construction but not design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T03:07:32-07:00","id":268125,"title":"","content":"The problem with the design is different from the one of the construction.<br /> <br /> Design is about creativity, you need to imagine a Manse, study the Dragon Lines and flows of Essence etc., see how it can all harmonize with the Demesne and so on. I don't think the Dragon-Blooded have Charms to boost creativity which is exactly what you need and that's what takes one month.<br /> <br /> If you get the original design of the manse you don't need the one month rule, you already have it, or perhaps a similar one to work from. Imagine it like an architect, it's the calculus and creativity that takes time, not drawing on paper. And the charms seem to boost the time and how well you do the drawing, the thinking you'll have to do on your own...<br /> <br /> In your place I would try to boost Occult and Lore through Excellencies and other insight charms to get a better understanding and convince the ST your superhuman levels of the abilities necessary for the design are a good reason for allowing the One Month Rule to be bent. Sometimes rules must follow the game and not the other way around, especially if a players is putting serious effort into it and coming up with logical and/or cool solutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2435,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","user":"Prophet","date":". 09-29-2014, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T04:52:32-07:00","id":268171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=267752#post267752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Essence 6+ god could feasibly use Chrysalis of Preservation to halt the manse's breakdown while you work, although it might take longer to find such a god and get them to do it than you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tien Yu is E6 and presmably has a vested interest in Lookshy not exploding. <br /> <br /> You could also summon a powerful elemental like Juritsu (or summon his Artisans and negotiate for is intervention).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T07:35:57-07:00","id":268257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=268125#post268125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the design is different from the one of the construction.<br /> <br /> Design is about creativity, you need to imagine a Manse, study the Dragon Lines and flows of Essence etc., see how it can all harmonize with the Demesne and so on. I don't think the Dragon-Blooded have Charms to boost creativity which is exactly what you need and that's what takes one month.<br /> <br /> If you get the original design of the manse you don't need the one month rule, you already have it, or perhaps a similar one to work from. Imagine it like an architect, it's the calculus and creativity that takes time, not drawing on paper. And the charms seem to boost the time and how well you do the drawing, the thinking you'll have to do on your own...</div> </div> </div> </div>What you described isn't really creativity. It's about math and engineering. Creativity is more about how aesthetically pleasing it is, imo. Which, sure, is a valid part of manse design. But the rest of it is the same as real-world surveying, environmental impact reports, CAD drawings, etc. There's no reason that I can think of why Crafting Charms should help with the actual building but not the drafting. Too much real-world logic being applied here. Solar CNNT lets you build a castle faster. How? Magic - no further explanation needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T09:02:11-07:00","id":268290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=268257#post268257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you described isn't really creativity. It's about math and engineering. Creativity is more about how aesthetically pleasing it is, imo. Which, sure, is a valid part of manse design. But the rest of it is the same as real-world surveying, environmental impact reports, CAD drawings, etc. There's no reason that I can think of why Crafting Charms should help with the actual building but not the drafting. Too much real-world logic being applied here. Solar CNNT lets you build a castle faster. How? Magic - no further explanation needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant it as a blend of both things, the aesthetical aspect of it and the eal-world surveying, environmental impact reports, CAD drawings, etc. And yes, I agree that everything that involves science can be sped up by charms, just not the creative process. But I don't agree that &quot;Magic&quot; is the answer for everything, you have to have some rules and base logic, that's why the game has charms and explanation for each charm.<br /> <br /> Breaking it down to an example: Frank Lloyd Wright's &quot;Hanna House&quot; <br /> <br /> Imagining Hanna House and drawing it on paper is pure creativity, making the necessary calculations to make it real an inhabitable is the part of the design where you can apply Craft Charms. Craft Charms won't boost your Creativity, but in my humble opinion, will speed up your calculation capacity and everything you need to translate the concept you imagined into a real thing.<br /> <br /> Despite charms making stuff happen because it's &quot;magic&quot; is not enough, that's why Manse Building has Lore and Occult minimums, there is a sense of logic built into Exalted Magic. Besides, if you read the charm descriptions, they enhance your working abilities, they don't make stuff appear of thin air, you still need materials and working hours.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:23:20-07:00","id":268326,"title":"","content":"Well, it's hard to rationalize something as CNNT working on a real-world principle aside from &quot;my hands just move really fast,&quot; but then that stops making sense when you need your whole body to build a brick wall but can still build that whole wall in like 3 minutes. It creates a (to me) goofy cartoonish image of moving really fast to build a wall.<br /> <br /> I don't think &quot;creativity&quot; is really a game mechanic, it's assumed you're not going to have writer's block or whatnot, or that that is folded in to the general process of calculations etc (which should be able to be sped up with Lore Charms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T17:20:09-07:00","id":268635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=268125#post268125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the design is different from the one of the construction.<br /> <br /> Design is about creativity, you need to imagine a Manse, study the Dragon Lines and flows of Essence etc., see how it can all harmonize with the Demesne and so on. I don't think the Dragon-Blooded have Charms to boost creativity which is exactly what you need and that's what takes one month.<br /> <br /> If you get the original design of the manse you don't need the one month rule, you already have it, or perhaps a similar one to work from. Imagine it like an architect, it's the calculus and creativity that takes time, not drawing on paper. And the charms seem to boost the time and how well you do the drawing, the thinking you'll have to do on your own...<br /> <br /> In your place I would try to boost Occult and Lore through Excellencies and other insight charms to get a better understanding and convince the ST your superhuman levels of the abilities necessary for the design are a good reason for allowing the One Month Rule to be bent. Sometimes rules must follow the game and not the other way around, especially if a players is putting serious effort into it and coming up with logical and/or cool solutions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thankyou very much! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Verang Astrologers, Lookshy Geomancers, Realm Sorcererous Engineers and [if I can find it] the Original manse design for Lookshy with Terristrial Occult/Lore Reinforcement should definately meet the 60 successes needed if it is termed an 'artiface' (as we're not making the whole manse from scratch).<br /> <br /> I also have the Singing Staff; so surely that can help.<br /> <br /> But, as I reread the comments-- Secondis first recommended capping the demense. Upon reflection I think this is exactly what we are doing. Albeit, with some fancy Sorcery and Astrology thrown in to make sure it doesn't explode (Long story, timey wimey freaking fae) making the capstones by RAW a level 3 artifact. <br /> <br /> COOL. This should totally be able to be done. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thankyou very much!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2556-firstaide","name":"Firstaide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T03:24:56-07:00","id":268899,"title":"","content":"Post the result! I'm curious now to whether you pull it off or not! Exalted is by definition achieving the impossible, I hope you nail it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T07:34:09-07:00","id":269016,"title":"","content":"Oh, you're depending on Sidereal astrology to do a good job? Welp, good luck with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T13:02:32-07:00","id":269398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=268125#post268125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the design is different from the one of the construction.<br /> <br /> Design is about creativity, you need to imagine a Manse, study the Dragon Lines and flows of Essence etc., see how it can all harmonize with the Demesne and so on. I don't think the Dragon-Blooded have Charms to boost creativity which is exactly what you need and that's what takes one month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, DB have one powerfull charm for this, allowing them to do in one day the equivalet of one week of intelluctual work : Elemental Concentration Transe. No prerequisite, Lore2/E1.<br /> One of the most usefull and eseaest DB charm to learn, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3053-ikumo","name":"Ikumo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T17:33:34-07:00","id":531414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=267413#post267413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To prevent a manse from exploding, as long as it's exploding due to geomantic reasons and not due to an inherent feature of the manse, all you need to do is place the appropriate capstones. Five of them, totally a Resources 5 cost, are placed at appropriate places, determined by a Perception + Lore roll at a difficulty of 1. That's it. No more explosion, you're free to work on the Manse, repairing it, for the months it requires, though proper repairs take far less time than actual construction.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=267413#post267413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post the result! I'm curious now to whether you pull it off or not! Exalted is by definition achieving the impossible, I hope you nail it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\"><b>HUZZAH!! It worked!</b></span><br /> <br /> I gave my GM a 14 page document written in character with page references and theories; and a diagram of Lookshy that had used GIS to calculate the 'right' places to put the capstones based on Jade affinities and occult law of fives. Thank you so much for all the assistance and charm ideas, it gave me a great idea where to look!<br /> <br /> My character made an Armilary Sphere to serve as the new manse heart; and the capstones all sympathetically linked back to it so when the energy fluctuated it pulsed to the capstones like a heart beating; and then the energy would flow back in. It took about 30 capstones to make these meridians; and a very large resources 5 donation of Orichalum to serve as the Heart of Lookshy. This is what is looks like:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.cultural-china.com/chinaWH/images/exbig_images/b30251df4531163189b26479f11bff57.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Those rings have celestial correspondences so when the Fae caused a Wibbly Woobly Timey Wimey (time collapsed) the sphere anchored the City to the only constant- the Stars.<br /> <br /> One of the other players was an astrologist (Thaumaturgy 1) so our GM had a puzzle for her to work out where the stars in Lookshy didn't match up to the Stars anywhere else. She had to figure out what stars where 'wrong' and realign everything to suit the fact that Lookshy as it was shouldn't exist. Clearly- Lookshy did exist tough - But HOW?! <br /> <br /> Through this puzzle, she discovered the Fae responsible for all the shenanigans and made a Codebreaker. Basically, every thaumaturgy ritual where it said &quot;the mask&quot; had to be replaced with &quot;the peacock&quot; (Two sessions more than that, but you get the idea). It was actually really cool; we had lots of paper and celestial maps and three of us were pouring over them trying to crack the code.<br /> <br /> Thank you if you are reading this, GM! Super fun problem solving with Stars.<br /> <br /> The capstones were completed and come calibration the manse disappeared along with every single WALL (Fae, you suck.) The city survived the sudden disappearance of its Manse/Capstone and only had to deal with the social implications of missing walls and disgruntled citizens/helotry. It wasn't attacked from anywhere else due to the Realm's army in position to stop anyone who would try to take advantage of the chaos. (Realm and Lookshy are allies in this game; or at least not hostile). Lookshy lives! EVER RESOLUTE!<br /> <br /> And- as a group we got to fight an Unshaped Raksha, in the middle of Creation, during a Cascading Years event. It had been washed in during the Balorian Crusade and when the Sword of Creation activated it hid itself by attaching itself to the manses of Deheleshen; feeding off the energy so it didn't disappear. We had to fight it's Graces; one of the Grace's being the Walls. Another, the Fourteenth (??) Infantry; Another, being Tu Yu. Hella cool.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the charm use for Terrestrials was all limited to 2-3 Essence. All of them charms used are listed below and are essence 2 or lower. Boo-yah! <br /> <br /> TLDR- Those who couldn't OCCULT at the problem were surrounded by those that could. Everyone helped each other boost abilities so it was all done in record time. Lookshy saved itself; we just showed them how.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>TERRESTRIAL(ABILITY) REINFORCEMENT</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 1m per 2 dice + 1m per subject;<br /> Mins: (Ability) 3, Essence 2;<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords: Combo-OK, Touch<br /> Duration: One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Any Excellency for the relevant Ability<br /> <br /> The two greatest strengths of the Dragon-Blooded have always been their superior numbers and their boundless capacity for teamwork. In the First Age, the Terrestrial Exalted were the unit commanders who led troops into battle under the direction of Celestial generals. In the modern era, Dragon-Blooded retain the capacity to elevate the mortals around them to greatness, if only temporarily. A Dragon-Blood with this Charm can improve the ratings of his allies in the relevant Ability for brief periods of time, effectively transferring the benefits of the First Excellency to another person for the duration of an entire scene. All allies to be affected must hold hands at the time of the Charm\u2019s activation.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood must spend one mote for every ally to be augmented and one mote for every two dice that are added to each person\u2019s rating in the relevant Ability. The maximum number of allies who can have their Ability ratings boosted at one time is equal to the Dragon-Blood\u2019s permanent Essence. The Charm has two limitations. First, no ally\u2019s Ability rating can be raised above the Ability rating of the Exalt who invokes this Charm. Second, no ally\u2019s Ability rating can be increased to more than twice its normal rating. Therefore, the ally must have at least one dot in the Ability for this Charm to affect him at all. The extra Ability dots apply for an entire scene for all purposes. If the augmented Ability affects one of the ally\u2019s DV ratings, the relevant DV should be recalculated for the duration of the scene. As is normal for dice-adding Charms, fractional motes left over by pool-size restrictions are lost.<br /> <br /> <b>ELEMENTAL CONCENTRATION TRANCE</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp;<br /> Mins: Lore 2, Essence 1;<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: One day<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> The simplest of Lore techniques exercised by the savants of Air, this Charm allows a character to meditate on her aligned element to temporarily augment her capacity to absorb knowledge. Provided that the Exalt has all the necessary research material handy, she can absorb a week\u2019s worth of study in a single day. She can continue to use this Charm on subsequent days, but if she uses it more days in a row than a number equal to her Lore trait, she suffers one level of unsoakable lethal damage for each extra day. The Exalt cannot heal this damage while under the effects of this Charm.<br /> <br /> <b>GEESE-FLYING-SOUTH ADMINISTRATION</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp;<br /> Mins: Bureaucracy 4, Essence 2;<br /> Type:Simple<br /> (Dramatic Action)<br /> Keywords: Compulsion, Social<br /> Duration: One task or three months (whichever is less)<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Confluence of Savant Thought<br /> <br /> While more martially inclined Dragon-Blooded look down on their kin in the bureaucracies and business centers, other Exalts understand that the business world can be as much a battlefield as any military setting. In such an environment, what matters is simply getting the job done. With this Charm, the Dragon-Blood can articulate a single task: tax collection, troop recruitment, merchandising transactions or almost anything else that can be accomplished in a bureaucratic setting. The task must be one that is bureaucratic in nature, however, and within the normal purview of the bureaucracy to be affected. That is, the Exalt could declare as a task \u201cacquire for me 2,000 straight swords\u201d but not \u201cconstruct for me 2,000 straight swords,\u201d as the latter instruction requires craftsmanship rather than bureaucratic acumen. Likewise, the Exalt could not order a tax-collection agency to engage in troop recruitment or to direct a mercenary company to completely reorganize a public library (at least, not without a fairly remarkable stunt).<br /> <br /> For the duration of the task, the Dragon-Blood\u2019s agents and assistants work with exceptional skill and dedication. The Exalt\u2019s player rolls (Charisma + Bureaucracy), adding his character\u2019s Essence in automatic successes. The Dragon-Blood must then assign the task to one or more mortal individuals who are in some way subservient to him (employees, military subordinates, junior clerks, etc.). Each mortal who is present when the task is assigned and whose highest MDV is less than the successes achieved on the dice roll instantly gains a loyalty toward quickly and efficiently completing the named task. Also, any affected mortal may add the Dragon-Blood\u2019s Essence to her MDV when resisting either natural or unnatural attempts to divert her from working to fulfill the task. Furthermore, the loyalty is contagious in nature. Even a mortal who is not present when the Dragon-Blood activates this Charm will gain both a loyalty toward completing the task and the MDV Essence bonus if he is assigned to work on it by a superior and his MDV is less than the Dragon-Blood\u2019s successes. The Charm\u2019s effects last until the task is complete or until three months have past, whichever comes first.<br /> <br /> The Charm can affect a given mortal only once for a single task, and if her MDV exceeds the Dragon-Blood\u2019s successes, she will be under no particular obligation to complete the task, nor will she gain any particular immunity against attempts to dissuade her. This does not mean that she cannot work freely on the task, which might be a normal part of her job, but she is not compelled to do so. On the other hand, if a mortal\u2019s MDV does not exceed the Dragon-Blood\u2019s successes, the mortal can resist only by spending a number of Willpower points equal to the Dragon-Blood\u2019s Essence.<br /> <br /> Mortals who are not affected by the Charm do not act as vectors for transmission of the contagious loyalty, but those who are can \u201cinfect\u201d new employees throughout the duration of the Charm.<br /> <br /> Exalted and spirits are utterly immune to the effects of Geese-Flying-South Administration, as are mortals who are not part of the affected bureaucracy. In addition to providing tangible protection for workers against sabotage by the Exalt\u2019s enemies, this Charm can also be used in the context of long social actions. By simply declaring the use of this Charm, the Dragon-Blood will fi nd at the conclusion of the task that the results are even better than he could have hoped.<br /> <br /> Monetary profits from the venture increase by an additional one percent per success on an (Intelligence + Bureaucracy) roll. The exchange of commodities results in an additional two percent more goods acquired per success on the roll. Conscription and other recruitment measures are likewise improved by two percent per success on a (Charisma + Bureaucracy) roll. Alternatively, instead of improving the success of the task, the Dragon-Blooded can choose to reduce the time it takes to complete the task. In such a case, each success on the relevant Bureaucracy roll reduces by five percent the amount of time it will take to complete a long-term bureaucratic endeavor. The Storyteller must determine the base result of any such endeavor before the improvements granted by the Charm are added. This Charm does not confer any long-term benefits on the efficiency of the bureaucracy in general. It simply makes sure that the bureaucracy will perform this single task with aplomb.<br /> <br /> <b>Flawless Training Execution</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 5 motes, 1 Willpower, plus 1 mote and 1 committed mote per fang trained<br /> Duration: Two months<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Minimum Performance: 2<br /> Minimum Essence: 2<br /> Prerequisite Charms: None<br /> <br /> This Charm allows the Dragon-Blooded to execute a training plan developed by Charms higher in this tree. With the Charm in effect, the Exalt can flawlessly lead drills, impart knowledge and teach classes without error. A single Dragon-Blooded can train a number of fangs equal to his Permanent Essence, but this Charm is synergistic \u2014 groups of Terrestrials working in concert can train large units of troops quickly. Each use of this Charm requires a training program or protocol developed with the Peerless Training Method Protocols or other Charms \u2014 a Dragon-Blooded can memorize a number of training programs at one time equal to his permanent Essence. While this Charm is in use, 1 mote of Essence per fang trained is committed to its continued operation \u2014 these motes are released when the program is complete.<br /> <br /> <b>Peerless Training Method Protocols</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 7 motes, 1 Willpower<br /> Duration: One month per dot of permanent Essence, or until training program is used<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Minimum Performance: 3<br /> Minimum Essence: 2<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Flawless Training Execution<br /> <br /> During the First Age, the Dragon-Blooded relied on the Celestial Exalted and their superior training methods to bring knowledge to the people and acted as facilitators, rather than designers, of training programs. When the Usurpation was being planned, the Terrestrial Exalted developed this family of Charms as a way to secretly train commandos and soldiers for their war, and the Dragon-Bloods have continued to refine the process ever since.<br /> <br /> Like the Sense-Destroying Methods, this Charm is actually a family of Charms that work in an identical fashion \u2014 five examples of the Charms available are listed in the Protocols sidebar on this page (Outcaste, pg 45) but others are known, and more can be developed as needed. Using one of these Charms, a skilled Dragon-Blood can develop a training program to improve those undergoing the program in specific areas \u2014 she can teach civilians how to be soldiers, teach disaster recovery techniques or impart the fundamentals of nearly any task.<br /> <br /> To use these Charms, the Terrestrial develops a training program \u2014 this requires one week, minus one day for each dot of permanent Essence over 2 (so a Dragon-Blooded with Essence 4 can develop a training program in five days). At the end of this time, the Charm\u2019s user commits the plan to record on paper, and his player rolls the character\u2019s Intelligence + Performance, against a difficulty of 4. If the Charm is successful, the plan will raise one Ability listed to 3, two Abilities to 2 and the remaining Abilities to 1 each, add one dot to an Attribute listed and raise one of the Virtues listed by one. Extra successes can be used to buy specialties for the Abilities raised \u2014 each extra success equals one specialty. No more than two specialties can be gained in this fashion. A failed roll indicates a training plan that simply will not work \u2014 the time and Essence spent is lost. A botched roll indicates a training plan that is subtly flawed in some fashion \u2014 it cannot work, but this will not become evident until it is implemented in the field by being used by someone with the Flawless Training Execution Charm. This will typically be noticeable within the first week of training, but particularly bad botches may take weeks to become evident.<br /> <br /> The Abilities gained by this Charm are not additive \u2014 if a character has more dots in that Ability than the training program would provide, she gains no benefit (though she may still gain any attached specialties, if she has less than three). These Charms cannot raise Attributes above 3, Virtues above 2 or Willpower above 8 (these stats can be raised later through experience). A given character can only benefit from a single Charm in this tree once but can be the recipient of multiple different Charms (so a character could receive the Combat Drill Protocol and then the Officer Readiness Training Protocol). This Charm has no effect whatsoever on individuals with an Essence higher than 1.<br /> <br /> Each training program is unique and can only be used once \u2014 if a developer wants to hand a training program to two subordinates, he must use this Charm twice and develop two different programs. A Dragon-Blooded can develop as many training programs as he likes, but each requires 2 committed motes of Essence to remain viable \u2014 these motes are returned when someone with the Flawless Training Execution Charm uses the training program.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2556-firstaide","name":"Firstaide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T04:22:14-07:00","id":531840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firstaide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help#post267348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue is the DESIGN rule. It says in the core book that to design a manse it takes a month MINIMUM (page 133). I have 10 days for it to be FINISHED.</div> </div> </div> </div>To hell with designing it, you are in Lookshy. A very large civilization with <i>lots</i> of people and <i>lots</i> of Exalted. Find a guy who designs Manses. Nab one of his Designs, use it to save the city.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Well, don't I feel like a stupid prick now. Carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T09:08:20-07:00","id":531994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=531840#post531840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To hell with designing it, you are in Lookshy. A very large civilization with <i>lots</i> of people and <i>lots</i> of Exalted. Find a guy who designs Manses. Nab one of his Designs, use it to save the city.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Well, don't I feel like a stupid prick now. Carry on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it actually work that way, tho?<br /> <br /> My understanding is that all manses are, by necessity, bespoke, because the point of a manse is to cap a demesne, and every demesne is different. You can't make a standardized design that works off the shelf, because even demesnes that are ostensibly exactly the same (a pair of Level 2 Water demesnes, for example) might have wildly differing essence flows and each will require their own specific geomantic designs to properly cap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T11:59:54-07:00","id":532104,"title":"","content":"@Firstaid <br /> <br /> First of all, congratulations for your job! Your creativity and hard work paid off and your contribution certainly made the game better <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Second, I want to thank you for sharing the end result but also the ideas and charms you came up with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> it really makes the community richer and might save another guy's skin someday eheh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T19:50:50-07:00","id":532694,"title":"","content":"Which of those charms are your inventions? <b>Flawless Training Execution </b>and <b>Peerless Training Method Protocols</b>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T16:01:51-07:00","id":533721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=532694#post532694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which of those charms are your inventions? <b>Flawless Training Execution </b>and <b>Peerless Training Method Protocols</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are from a website that lists bunches of charms, Firstaide didn't realise they were not in the book. Most of the site is 100% cannon for 2.5 but some custom stuff is slipped in there as well.<br /> <br /> That said, it was more effort, creativity and fun that got the whole thing working and won me over than any specific hard-rule mechanic. Session(s) were fun, nice to see it was appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T09:04:15-07:00","id":534430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=533721#post533721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it was more effort, creativity and fun that got the whole thing working and won me over than any specific hard-rule mechanic</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to like this more than once! THIS is how any and every RPG should be played! I'm lucky to play with a group of friends for over 10 years. The story and fun always comes first even if we have to trump over the rules <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T05:07:30-07:00","id":535468,"title":"","content":"I wish I had checked this thread sooner. As it happens there is a combination that might have suited you better than the above custom training Charms.<br /> <br /> The War Charm From Eggs to (Element) Dragons from Thousand Correct Actions is a Charm that is easy to write off as useless. When used to train mortals it is limited by season, takes a long time to train and can only train a limited number of abilities to a limited degree.<br /> <br /> However, with the assistance of a Celestial Exalt it becomes vastly better. With repurchases or several trainers acting in concert, it can train all Abilities, Specialities, Virtues, Willpower and most Attributes to a limit only of the trainer's traits. In some cases it is even more effective than Solar training Charms thanks to its sheer versatility. Its only real downside is that unlike Solar training Charms it has an upper limit of students at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 06-01-2015, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T06:31:40-07:00","id":535513,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but if you accept the help of foul Anathema, is there even any point in winning anymore? Haven't you just become the bad guys?<br /> <br /> Anyway, when you run the training system for the realm, it's not that hard to cycle troops through different trainers on a seasonal basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T08:26:36-07:00","id":535621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/267348-dragon-blood-charms-help?p=535513#post535513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but if you accept the help of foul Anathema, is there even any point in winning anymore? Haven't you just become the bad guys?<br /> <br /> Anyway, when you run the training system for the realm, it's not that hard to cycle troops through different trainers on a seasonal basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>OP is playing an Eclipse on a time limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}